Here is a basic example of an Autocomplete component using React without relying on other third-party packages:
```
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ options, onSelected }) => {
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [suggestions, setSuggestions] = useState([]);
  const [activeSuggestionIndex, setActiveSuggestionIndex] = useState(-1);

  useEffect(() => {
    const filteredSuggestions = options.filter((option) => {
      return option.toLowerCase().includes(inputValue.toLowerCase());
    });

    setSuggestions(filteredSuggestions);
  }, [inputValue, options]);

  const handleInputChange = (e) => {
    setInputValue(e.target.value);
  };

  const handleSelectSuggestion = (e) => {
    onSelected(suggestions[activeSuggestionIndex]);
  };

  const handleArrowNavigation = (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      setActiveSuggestionIndex(activeSuggestionIndex - 1);
    } else if (e.key === 'ArrowDown') {
      setActiveSuggestionIndex(activeSuggestionIndex + 1);
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={inputValue}
        onChange={handleInputChange}
        onFocus={() => setActiveSuggestionIndex(0)}
        onKeyDown={handleArrowNavigation}
      />
      <ul>
        {suggestions.map((suggestion, index) => (
          <li
            key={index}
            className={activeSuggestionIndex === index ? 'active-suggestion' : ''}
            onClick={() => {
              handleSelectSuggestion({});
              setInputValue(suggestion);
              setActiveSuggestionIndex(-1);
            }}
          >
            {suggestion}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
};

export default Autocomplete;
```
This component takes two props:

* `options`: an array of options to be autocompleted
* `onSelected`: a function to be called when a suggestion is selected

The component maintains three state variables:

* `inputValue`: the current value of the input field
* `suggestions`: an array of filtered options based on the input value
* `activeSuggestionIndex`: the index of the currently active suggestion

When the input field is changed, the component filters the options and updates the `suggestions` state. When an arrow key is pressed, the component updates the `activeSuggestionIndex` state. When a suggestion is clicked, the component calls the `onSelected` function and updates the `inputValue` and `activeSuggestionIndex` states.

